-- title:
--   Unramifiedness of valuation rings of the Hecke roof field
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ given by [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the subfield generated over $L$ by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ the set `intFormRatiosC` attached to $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with $\varpi \in A$ generating the maximal ideal; $K$ carries an $A$-algebra structure compatible with $A \to L \to K$, and $j \in K$ is a nonzero element whose Laurent expansion is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{numerator series})$ of the $j$-invariant. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \ne p$, and let $K_\ell$ be the analogous subfield [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p) (M * p * ℓ))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), built from $\Gamma_1(Mp) \cap \Gamma_0(Mp\ell)$, again an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K_\ell$, and let $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ be nonzero with the same $q$-expansion. The conclusion: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ such that the image of $A$ lies in $V$, the image of the maximal ideal of $A$ lies in the nonunits of $V$, and $P(j_\ell)$ together with $P(j_\ell)^{-1}$ lies in $V$ for every $P \in A[X]$ whose reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ is nonzero, one has $x \cdot (\varpi)^{-1} \in V$ for every nonunit $x$ of $V$; equivalently the maximal ideal of $V$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, so $V$ is unramified over $A$.
--
--   This is the statement that the special fibre over $A$ of the two-chart model of the Hecke roof field of level $\Gamma_1(Mp) \cap \Gamma_0(Mp\ell)$, in the case $\ell \neq p$, is generically reduced: every valuation ring of the roof field lying over the maximal ideal of $A$ and unramified along the generic $j$-line has ramification index one. It feeds the reducedness statement [`ModularCurve.XOneP.isReduced_pullback_heckeDegeneracy_baseChange_specialFibre_component_of_ne_of_specializes_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.isReduced_pullback_heckeDegeneracy_baseChange_specialFibre_component_of_ne_of_specializes_twoChartModel_x1_mul), and is deduced from the corresponding factorisation statement [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_eq_mul_of_mem_nonunits_valuationSubring_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_eq_mul_of_mem_nonunits_valuationSubring_x1_mul) at level $\Gamma_1(Mp)$.
